# The ONE filter on the image build context (the CDK DockerImageAsset context is the repo
# root). It is an ALLOWLIST: exclude everything, then re-include only what the Dockerfile
# COPYs. A new root file (STATUS.md, an AI-DLC record, .coverage) therefore never enters the
# context, never moves the image asset hash, and never redeploys an arm (T-PKG-U3-14/-15).
# It also cannot recreate the recursive infra/cdk.out self-copy (ENAMETOOLONG) a denylist
# miss once caused.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: later patterns win. The re-exclusions must come after the `!` lines.
# Any new serving path must be added here in the same commit as the Dockerfile COPY for it.
*
!src/
!config/
!pyproject.toml
!requirements-agent.txt
!Dockerfile
# U6 P-U6-8: no request-path module reads the artifact location file (only the publisher
# does), so it stays out of the image and a serving_form edit cannot move the asset hash.
config/artifact-location.json
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.egg-info
